[{:db/id "q-83897/selection/3ab526f8ccfb323626f5e1042005ebbf0898255a3c4b5c17792d7f935d9120a7" :answer/id #uuid "2acd023d-e5ef-51a4-a3ff-d156d6e7c954" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "29\\,991" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83897/selection/a0bc66fe854f423a66a454a8e0589212ca3b76c9fbd1d1cbb8c149feab5dc902" :answer/id #uuid "30ef881e-ee66-54fa-add7-32f98a5b45e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37\\,993" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83897/selection/663b1dd0e76f7a8c3b2b786302e685d29b0c8eb03acb93712b1833ab3a58dd90" :answer/id #uuid "924ae145-7d83-5ca5-aeea-ad3e9862a49a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49\\,009" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83897/selection/e6af66cc46cdd774133aa869f27ec8ebaa10e5df7de6fdd4626998f1ee48c2ba" :answer/id #uuid "52ef7166-6414-5431-9370-76d6875572b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31\\,284" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83897/selection/713b44408dafa148a5827ef24ab071f6fe18769eca81b73020bc695d6002f0d1" :answer/id #uuid "621443f9-3335-56f4-bafc-f82e6c769593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48\\,701" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83897/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18b07d44-e3d4-5446-b48b-3f1070f6af15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83897/selection/663b1dd0e76f7a8c3b2b786302e685d29b0c8eb03acb93712b1833ab3a58dd90" :answer-field/choices ["q-83897/selection/3ab526f8ccfb323626f5e1042005ebbf0898255a3c4b5c17792d7f935d9120a7" "q-83897/selection/a0bc66fe854f423a66a454a8e0589212ca3b76c9fbd1d1cbb8c149feab5dc902" "q-83897/selection/663b1dd0e76f7a8c3b2b786302e685d29b0c8eb03acb93712b1833ab3a58dd90" "q-83897/selection/e6af66cc46cdd774133aa869f27ec8ebaa10e5df7de6fdd4626998f1ee48c2ba" "q-83897/selection/713b44408dafa148a5827ef24ab071f6fe18769eca81b73020bc695d6002f0d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83897" :question/id #uuid "2763d23a-b642-55a2-bdf1-afa0ee05a7f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-83897" :question/problem "The growth rate of the hedgehog population $P(t)$ in a certain forest is jointly proportional to the hedgehog population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the forest's carrying capacity and the hedgehog population. The constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,005$ and the carrying capacity is $50\\,000.$ How many hedgehogs will there be in the forest after $20$ years given that there were $12\\,500$ hedgehogs initially? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since the hedgehog population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the hedgehog population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the hedgehog population, the hedgehog population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,005,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=50\\,000.$ Therefore, the hedgehog population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,005P(50\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{50\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(50\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,005)t}}=\\frac{50\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.25t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=12\\,500$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =12\\,500 \\\\ \\frac{50\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.25(0)}} & =12\\,500 \\\\ 1+C & =4 \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{50\\,000}{1+3{e}^{-0.25\\cdot t}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=20$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(20) & =\\frac{50\\,000}{1+3{e}^{-0.25\\cdot 20}} \\\\  & ≈49\\,009.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83897/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83897"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172/selection/cbdf470d0bbb5cd75bc195577f9a579ff0a79fbc6d1416e79461bc32caecf002" :answer/id #uuid "886d101f-a639-5896-be9d-c8f1f0f8d6ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-0.25t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172/selection/d5f922e6fbf2aa5f2e5e85a5966048a961af42aaf0d147f02f99da3781331474" :answer/id #uuid "3aa225bc-90b4-5073-8ea3-a5d6044b148b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{100}{1+5{e}^{-0.25t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172/selection/c7abb1641e6919e49a64fcc59466b9dc8281cede955821723e5f18289b4fb47c" :answer/id #uuid "55a7c007-0db8-5c63-9c35-5a93b9292c74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{1\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-2.5t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172/selection/c4626a46b2082a1dc361035840e0f7be96b3f852bd2f00ddca1c86f2b00a5457" :answer/id #uuid "c85ec9ea-792d-53b0-8697-fd10f261443e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-5t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172/selection/6bc457e208e4572c4b8201e7afce385a382875ef2687bb630369d831db596a5a" :answer/id #uuid "8d428ced-a555-5bff-9dda-35498abbf304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{1\\,000}{1+199{e}^{-0.25t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "94d4d33f-4dde-5728-a0fc-d4cacbe5a7a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84172/selection/cbdf470d0bbb5cd75bc195577f9a579ff0a79fbc6d1416e79461bc32caecf002" :answer-field/choices ["q-84172/selection/cbdf470d0bbb5cd75bc195577f9a579ff0a79fbc6d1416e79461bc32caecf002" "q-84172/selection/d5f922e6fbf2aa5f2e5e85a5966048a961af42aaf0d147f02f99da3781331474" "q-84172/selection/c7abb1641e6919e49a64fcc59466b9dc8281cede955821723e5f18289b4fb47c" "q-84172/selection/c4626a46b2082a1dc361035840e0f7be96b3f852bd2f00ddca1c86f2b00a5457" "q-84172/selection/6bc457e208e4572c4b8201e7afce385a382875ef2687bb630369d831db596a5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84172" :question/id #uuid "2693e3d3-c911-502b-af47-4d7552962708" :question/math-academy-id "q-84172" :question/problem "The growth rate of the hamster population $P(t)$ in the Pets' Corner pet shop is jointly proportional to the hamster population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between Pets' Corner's carrying capacity and the hamster population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.002\\,5$ and the carrying capacity is $100,$ then find an expression for the hamster population after $t$ years, given that there were $5$ hamsters in the pets' corner initially." :question/worked-solution "Since the hamster population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the hamster population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the hamster population, the hamster population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality $k=0.002\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=100.$ Therefore, the hamster population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.002\\,5P(100-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-(100\\cdot 0.002\\,5)t}}=\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-0.25t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=5$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-0.25\\cdot 0}} & =5 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\ C & =20-1 \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-0.25t}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-84172/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84172"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862/selection/b6f8e8bc07b3de7376a16c56568bab2f6e885e3c45571115b078fc09cb8912ca" :answer/id #uuid "62db0577-451a-5fa3-bc70-eb68d3959725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.0008t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862/selection/4f01dc660a84c66d7b9b01ea72d956b20a0a9921d31e1151bff7539b57d50a7a" :answer/id #uuid "f45bdf98-6a38-51f7-a5fa-f5b869a45762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{7}{1+{e}^{-t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862/selection/8eec60c62f001bc530d2f82ea424faa8f3dcc5837786066d0458eb186317bd7d" :answer/id #uuid "7e997a0f-0b1a-5387-8c64-16a96d2a27e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{2\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-12.8t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862/selection/5275906337a0a061d7ee317910513961ee51bfd9d43795b1889343b182c25583" :answer/id #uuid "b36ea38c-14b8-5073-b82b-a46ac244e1ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{16\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-0.0008t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862/selection/b2293eff5b88f24822756477cd58dc114de416ca19f5b6efa174039d81a5a890" :answer/id #uuid "4a5b1506-e4d5-51d8-9e6b-398e41f8b696" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{16\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-12.8t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd83806b-f149-5a17-9b3b-963420bcf146" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119862/selection/b2293eff5b88f24822756477cd58dc114de416ca19f5b6efa174039d81a5a890" :answer-field/choices ["q-119862/selection/b6f8e8bc07b3de7376a16c56568bab2f6e885e3c45571115b078fc09cb8912ca" "q-119862/selection/4f01dc660a84c66d7b9b01ea72d956b20a0a9921d31e1151bff7539b57d50a7a" "q-119862/selection/8eec60c62f001bc530d2f82ea424faa8f3dcc5837786066d0458eb186317bd7d" "q-119862/selection/5275906337a0a061d7ee317910513961ee51bfd9d43795b1889343b182c25583" "q-119862/selection/b2293eff5b88f24822756477cd58dc114de416ca19f5b6efa174039d81a5a890"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119862" :question/id #uuid "8d253187-80b1-5861-b58e-9ee40c0dee55" :question/math-academy-id "q-119862" :question/problem "The growth rate of the flamingo population $P(t)$ in in a certain lagoon is jointly proportional to the flamingo population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the lagoon's carrying capacity and the flamingo population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,8$ and the carrying capacity is $16\\,000,$ then find an expression for the flamingo population after $t$ years, given that there were $2\\,000$ flamingos in the lagoon initially." :question/worked-solution "Since the flamingo population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the flamingo population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the flamingo population, the flamingo population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,8,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=16\\,000.$ Therefore, the flamingo population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,8P(16\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{16\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(16\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,8)t}}=\\frac{16\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-12.8t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=2\\,000$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-12.8\\cdot 0}} & =2\\,000 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{16\\,000}{2\\,000} \\\\ C & =8-1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{16\\,000}{1+7{e}^{-12.8t}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e71ba74-f952-56ef-885c-a32c4a4aec20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353260/field-1/39a5ce6df648355b801d1b8ecb4c5f4f609af8f07bae4fac68affda9cbedd111" :answer/id #uuid "d334077c-beef-56ce-9979-2701439fc631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "145" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353260/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "60219ad4-7db9-5231-8618-931926cf48b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353260/field-1/39a5ce6df648355b801d1b8ecb4c5f4f609af8f07bae4fac68affda9cbedd111" :answer-field/choices ["q-353260/field-1/39a5ce6df648355b801d1b8ecb4c5f4f609af8f07bae4fac68affda9cbedd111"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353260" :question/id #uuid "c381b932-131a-52b6-a703-235e81782234" :question/math-academy-id "q-353260" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of insects in a greenhouse follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.6P-0.002{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in days. If there were $40$ insects in the greenhouse initially, how many insects were in the greenhouse after $3$ days? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nAfter $3$ days, approximately\n{{field-1}} insects were in the greenhouse." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.6P-0.002{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.002P(300-P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.002,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=300.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{300}{1+C{e}^{-(300\\cdot 0.002)t}}=\\frac{300}{1+C{e}^{-0.6t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=40$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{300}{1+C{e}^{-0.6(0)}} & =40 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{300}{40} \\\\ C & =7.5-1 \\\\  & =6.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{300}{1+6.5{e}^{-0.6t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=3$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =\\frac{300}{1+6.5{e}^{-0.6(3)}} \\\\  & ≈145.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ days, approximately $145$ insects were in the greenhouse." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353260/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353263/field-1/9d8e9bb16bbe077c11b53cfaa48ab1c9bbe2756ec8245e2a00d51ea4eb476196" :answer/id #uuid "611bddd3-80d2-53f1-b1ad-4f2c2bcaf9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1295" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353263/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d20b2304-57a5-5622-98a5-f03e0b13d033" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353263/field-1/9d8e9bb16bbe077c11b53cfaa48ab1c9bbe2756ec8245e2a00d51ea4eb476196" :answer-field/choices ["q-353263/field-1/9d8e9bb16bbe077c11b53cfaa48ab1c9bbe2756ec8245e2a00d51ea4eb476196"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353263" :question/id #uuid "c6dfd46a-5e47-5cc5-b3ca-74e6340d301d" :question/math-academy-id "q-353263" :question/problem "The population $P(t)$ of customers using a new ride-share service in a city follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.18P-0.000\\,12{P}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in months. If there were $900$ customers using the service initially, how many customers were using the service after $8$ months? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nAfter $8$ months, approximately\n{{field-1}} customers were using the service." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.18P-0.000\\,12{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,12P(1500-P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.00012,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=1500.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1500}{1+C{e}^{-(1500\\cdot 0.000\\,12)t}}=\\frac{1500}{1+C{e}^{-0.18t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=900$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1500}{1+C{e}^{-0.18(0)}} & =900 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{1500}{900} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{3}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1500}{1+\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-0.18t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=8$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8) & =\\frac{1500}{1+\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-0.18(8)}} \\\\  & ≈1295.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $8$ months, approximately $1295$ customers were using the service." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353263/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18af80e5-cd0f-5a1d-b299-2956fd886c5d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
